 "notes": "All five planned kinds kept. Mattock: dropped A.M. Leonard Cutter/Pick Mattock trade SKUs (scope rule); pick and cutter mattock kept as maker-free archetypes; Hoedag, DeWit and Sneeboer models kept in m. Old Freund maker recorded as Freund Victoria (retrieved page). Niwaki Golden Spade sourced from a retailer page (niwaki.com returned 403). Not added for lack of a retrievable page this session: Krumpholz specific spade models beyond the Spitzspaten line and its founding year; Clarington Forge/Bulldog named models; Meadow Creature tall broadfork (429); a Gardener's broadfork pattern; manure fork as archetype (kept as type). Snow and coal shovels left to other shelves/out. No traditions: no artisan tradition beyond the Irish loy, which is an archetype."
}